Z||000000||hugh||10-01-2000||08:48 PM||||I am going to use Ryanes tubular front end  and struts with coilovers.The wheels I have on the car now stick out of the wheel wells between 1 and 2 inches.I want to go to a bigger tire/wheel combination in the rear.I need to know what the stock track is for my 88,front and rear.I prefer the tires inside the front wheel well if that was their original location.I bought the car with these wheels,so I don't know exactly where the wheels should fall and I haven't seen any other cars in my area to compare to.My concern is with a wider track,how much more stress is put on the front end components?If I need to change wheels I will,then these wheels will be sold.One more thing,where can I go to find nice wheels for my car. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/hugh_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||10-01-2000||09:42 PM||||Hugh, <BR>From Corbin's Fiero Spotters guide...<P>Tread (track?), front<P>  84-87     57.8<BR>  88 coupe  59.3<BR>  88 GT     59.7<P>Tread, rear<P>  84-87     58.7<BR>  88 coupe  59.4<BR>  88 GT     60.1<P>If you need an exact measurement (from a Formula), let me know. Specify where you want the measurements taken.<BR> <P><BR> <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (soon to receive transplant.)<BR>88 "pretzeled" Formula <P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 10-01-2000).]||||reg||1
